.TH SPLIT 1
.SH NAME
split \- split a file into pieces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "split [ \-n ] [ file [ name ] ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B split
reads
.I file
and writes it in
.I n
line pieces (default 1000), as many as necessary, onto a set of output files.
The name of the first output file is
.I name
with
.B aa
appended, and so on lexicographically.
If no output name is given,
.B x
is default.
.PP
If no input file is given, or if `\-' is given in its stead, then the standard input file is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
To split files
.I lnames
into segments of 17 lines calling each one
.IR partialaa ,
.IR partialab ,
etc.
.RS
.nf
split \-17 lnames partial
.fi
.RE
.sp
